          "text": "{\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"This is a direct, emphatic avowal presented as true in answer to Maria’s concern that his present feelings might be temporary or imagined.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt end for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig.\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.93,\"reason\":\"The focal words themselves avow a present state and do not undertake a specified action or obligation. A commitment to a shared life appears in the separate neighbouring sentence and should not be transferred to the target.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Du er den, jeg vil dø med, men først vil jeg leve meget, meget længe med Dig.\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.91,\"reason\":\"Although the reunion is highly emotional, the expression is delivered as a reasoned answer to Maria’s question, not as a reflex-like or uncontrolled affective discharge.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg svarer: »Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt end for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig.\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.9,\"reason\":\"The target’s core force is adequately represented as an emphatic truth-presenting avowal of love; no distinct residual function is textually required.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"At an emotional reunion, Maria asks whether his changed attitude is genuine, lasting, and not something he will regret the next day. He answers by emphatically declaring that he loves her and then separately describes enduring love and a desired shared life.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"present\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"The target itself contains no clear undertaking. In the neighbouring statement, the male speaker projects or undertakes a long shared life with Maria: “Du er den, jeg vil dø med, men først vil jeg leve meget, meget længe med Dig.” Maria’s tears and happiness indicate favourable reception of the overall declaration, but the supplied passage gives no explicit verbal acceptance or precise terms for that undertaking.\",\"recognised_work\":false,\"recognition_note\":\"I do not recognize the work from the supplied text alone.\",\"limitations\":\"The passage strongly supports the avowal’s represented sincerity, including the narrator’s statement that Maria understands he speaks truth. It does not establish formal terms, the exact status of the relationship after this exchange, or an explicit uptake of the neighbouring shared-life commitment.\"}"
